{{define "content"}}

<h1>Set up {{.StoreName}}</h1>

<p>There is no administrator account yet. The server printed a one-time setup token
to its log when it started — <code>docker compose logs server</code>, or wherever
this deployment's logs go — and it is what authorises this first account.</p>

<form method="post" action="/admin/setup">
  {{template "csrf" .CSRFToken}}

  <fieldset class="panel">
    <legend>Setup token</legend>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="token">Token</label>
      {{/* Never re-filled after a failed attempt: it is a credential, and a value
           the browser remembers is one that turns up in form history and in a
           screenshot of this page. */}}
      <input id="token" name="token" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" autofocus required>
      {{template "err" index .Errors "token"}}
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <fieldset class="panel">
    <legend>Your account</legend>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="email">Email</label>
      <input id="email" type="email" name="email" value="{{.Email}}"
             autocomplete="username" autocapitalize="none" required>
      {{template "err" index .Errors "email"}}
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="name">Name</label>
      <input id="name" name="name" value="{{.Name}}" autocomplete="name">
      {{template "err" index .Errors "name"}}
      <small class="hint">Optional. Shown instead of your address wherever the admin
      names you.</small>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="password">Password</label>
      <input id="password" type="password" name="password" autocomplete="new-password" required>
      {{template "err" index .Errors "password"}}
      <small class="hint">At least 12 characters. Length is the only rule: a short
      passphrase beats a mangled word.</small>
    </div>
    <div class="field">
      <label for="password_confirm">Confirm password</label>
      <input id="password_confirm" type="password" name="password_confirm"
             autocomplete="new-password" required>
      {{template "err" index .Errors "password_confirm"}}
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  <div class="actions">
    <button type="submit">Create administrator</button>
  </div>
</form>

<p><small>This account is the store's <strong>owner</strong>: it can create other
administrators, and it cannot be disabled or demoted while it is the only enabled
owner. The setup token is spent the moment this succeeds, and this page stops
existing.</small></p>

{{end}}
